    "kind": "news",
    "check": "returned unopposed: 'Seven Unionists have been nominated for each of the Central and East Wards, showing one change from the present Council membership — Mr. James Henderson for Mr. Joseph Patton, who is retiring — but there will be a contest in the East Ward also' (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1967, p. 5, image read). The Belfast Telegraph (4 May 1967, p. 11, image read) names the fourteen Unionists without wards; the seven elected at the East Ward poll (Belfast News-Letter, 18 May 1967, p. 2) leave these seven, who are the 1964 Central Ward members with Henderson in place of Patton.",
