  "note": "Election of the Dungannon Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 17 May 1967. Central Ward was not polled: seven Unionists were nominated for its seven seats (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1967, p. 5). The ward is assigned by elimination: the Belfast Telegraph (4 May 1967, p. 11) lists the fourteen Unionist nominees for the Central and East Wards together, and the other seven were elected at the East Ward poll. The six sitting members are the 1964 Central Ward members; the paper prints 'R. Brown' where the 1961 and 1964 Central Ward results print J. Brown. Returned unopposed."
